WEBVTT

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.340
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What animal would you most like to see in the wild,

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.240
for example, on a safari?

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.233
<v><b>Hope:</b></v> Oh, that’s a really good question.

00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:20.637
Probably an elephant.

00:00:20.766 --> 00:00:21.304
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Why?

00:00:21.398 --> 00:00:22.681
<v><b>Hope:</b></v> I think they’re amazing.

00:00:22.918 --> 00:00:30.320
They’re so big, and just, they sort of live in the wilderness, and yeah.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.540
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have a phobia?

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.420
<v><b>Mairi:</b></v> I’m frightened of spiders.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.300
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How long have you had it?

00:00:46.387 --> 00:00:50.660
<v><b>Mairi:</b></v> Er, since I was about five or six I think, but I’m not sure.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.820
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How does it affect your life?

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:59.860
<v><b>Mairi:</b></v> Um, I normally have to check a room to see if there’s a big spider in it

00:00:59.861 --> 00:01:04.686
before I go to sleep, because, one time a spider, er, joined me in my bed.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.020
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Who’s the oldest person you know well?

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.620
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> My great aunt is a hundred and four, living in California.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.100
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of life has she had?

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.622
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> She has had a great life.

00:01:30.958 --> 00:01:34.780
She’s still travelling at a hundred and four.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.420
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you do any sport or exercise?

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.820
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> I run and I hike, and I do yoga.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.020
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you enjoy it?

00:01:52.673 --> 00:01:54.857
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> I love hiking, hiking is my favourite,

00:01:54.857 --> 00:01:57.561
and I just love being in nature and outdoors,

00:01:57.561 --> 00:01:59.860
and experiencing nature on foot.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.420
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Are you a morning or evening person?

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.363
<v><b>Kathy:</b></v> Um, I’m a morning person.

00:02:08.405 --> 00:02:12.293
Um, I feel a lot more awake in the morning than in the evening, um,

00:02:12.318 --> 00:02:16.740
so I tend to get up early, even when I’m not at, even when I’m not at work.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.580
Um, and I prefer to go to bed earlier.